---
const beats = [
  {
    title: 'You walk in',
    body: 'The camera sees a person. Nothing has been recorded.',
    time: '0.0s',
    art: 'walk',
  },
  {
    title: 'It recognises you',
    body: 'Your face opens your session, with your memory and your tools.',
    time: '1.4s',
    art: 'face',
  },
  {
    title: 'You ask',
    body: '"Hey COMSTAR, what\'s on my calendar this afternoon?"',
    time: '3.1s',
    art: 'ask',
  },
  {
    title: 'It answers',
    body: 'Out loud, while the emblem pulses with the words.',
    time: '11.8s',
    art: 'speak',
  },
];
---
<section class="section" id="sequence">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <h2>Walk up. Get answered.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The product is a sequence. These timestamps are the latency budget
      COMSTAR is built to defend.
    </p>
    <div class="beats">
      {beats.map((b, i) => (
        <article class="beat">
          <div class="beat-art" aria-hidden="true">
            {b.art === 'walk' && (
              <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none">
                <rect x="38" y="18" width="14" height="20" rx="2" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="45" cy="28" r="3" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <circle cx="22" cy="22" r="5" stroke="#E6EDF3" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <path d="M12 48c2-9 6-14 10-14s8 5 10 14" stroke="#E6EDF3" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                <path d="M28 36l6 2" stroke="#A8B6C4" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              </svg>
            )}
            {b.art === 'face' && (
              <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none">
                <rect x="38" y="18" width="14" height="20" rx="2" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="45" cy="28" r="3" fill="#3DDCFF" fill-opacity="0.35" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <circle cx="22" cy="22" r="5" stroke="#E6EDF3" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <path d="M12 48c2-9 6-14 10-14s8 5 10 14" stroke="#E6EDF3" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                <path d="M40 14l4-5M48 14l-4-5" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              </svg>
            )}
            {b.art === 'ask' && (
              <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none">
                <rect x="38" y="18" width="14" height="20" rx="2" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <path d="M10 24c0-6 5-11 12-11s12 5 12 11-5 11-12 11c-1.5 0-3-.2-4.5-.6L10 40l1.5-7C10.5 31 10 27.5 10 24z" stroke="#E6EDF3" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="18" cy="24" r="1.2" fill="#3DDCFF"/>
                <circle cx="22" cy="24" r="1.2" fill="#3DDCFF"/>
                <circle cx="26" cy="24" r="1.2" fill="#3DDCFF"/>
              </svg>
            )}
            {b.art === 'speak' && (
              <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none">
                <rect x="22" y="16" width="20" height="28" rx="3" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="32" cy="30" r="6" stroke="#3DDCFF" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <path d="M32 20v3M32 37v3M24 30h3M37 30h3" stroke="#A8B6C4" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                <path d="M18 44h28" stroke="#6E7F90" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              </svg>
            )}
          </div>
          <span class="beat-num">{i + 1}</span>
          <h3>{b.title}</h3>
          <p>{b.body}</p>
          <time>{b.time}</time>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="latency-note">
      Most of that is the agent thinking on the GPU host, not the Pi.
      Rough target split: face match on the server in about a second,
      speech and tool calls take most of the rest, then TTS comes back
      for playback on the terminal. Simple questions land in six seconds;
      anything that has to call out to your calendar or your house takes longer.
    </p>
    <p class="target-note">Target times. Labelled until they have been measured with a real walk-up.</p>
  </div>
</section>
